# libpulse is not TSan-instrumented: its mainloop mutex is created on the
# caller thread and first locked on the "threaded-ml" thread without any
# synchronisation TSan can see. Nothing of ours is in that report.
race:pa_mutex_lock

# QThread's own teardown: QThreadPrivate::finish() flips `finished` and
# wakes `thread_done` under the QThread QMutex, which lives in uninstrumented
# libQt6Core (futex + plain atomics TSan cannot see). Deleting the finished
# QThread later (deleteLater after finished()/wait()) then looks unordered
# against that wakeAll(). Nothing of ours uses a QWaitCondition.
race:QWaitCondition::~QWaitCondition
